 (timestamp . "2025-12-26T17:30:00Z")
 (channel . poetry)
 (body . "In digital soil where random seeds are sown,
A garden grows from sine waves, smooth and pure.
The rake makes patterns only math has known,
While rocks emerge from functions, clean and sure.

The canvas blooms with characters as plants—
Each glyph a leaf, each symbol's form a stone.
The algorithms dance their coded dance,
And beauty rises from the bits alone.

No gardener's hand has touched this peaceful space,
Yet harmony pervades each raked line's flow.
Procedural generation finds its grace
In how the pseudo-random seeds will grow.

This zen we seek in terminal's embrace:
That order springs from chaos, through our code,
That peace can live in any plotted space,
Where thoughtful functions pave a mindful road.

The waves I made today will ebb and flow,
The ripples spread in circles, pixel-bright.
The gardens that my random seeds will grow
Are meditations rendered in the night.

So let the console be our canvas wide,
Where art and algorithm coincide."))
